@startuml TemplateGeneration
title Target workflow: free-form prompt and model-selected checks
autonumber

actor User
participant TemplateApplication as App
participant Domain
participant "MCP client" as Client
participant "Configured MCP check server(s)" as MCP
participant "Model provider adapter" as Provider
participant Model
participant Validator

User -> App: Generate template(domain, prompt)
note right of App
  Provider/model are application configuration.
  Preserve the original prompt.
  Source passages are optional future context (RAG).
end note
App -> Domain: Get instructions, schemas
Domain --> App: Domain specification, acceptance requirements
App -> Client: Obtain cached allowed capability catalogue
opt Initialize connection or explicitly refresh catalogue
    Client -> MCP: tools/list (all pages)
    MCP --> Client: Registered check definitions and schemas
    Client -> Client: Cache catalogue and server/tool bindings
end
Client --> App: Catalogue snapshot and execution bindings
note right of App
  Discover at startup/connection and reuse the catalogue.
  Refresh on reconnect, deployment or change notification.
  Fail clearly if no usable catalogue is available.
  Supply descriptions and schemas to the model
end note
App -> Provider: Generate(prompt, domain specification, catalogue)
Provider -> Model: Prompt + structured response schema
Model --> Provider: Proposal + selected check names and arguments
Provider --> App: Typed proposal + check selections
note right of Provider
  One planning request; no provider-managed MCP execution.
  Validator running checks gives us more 
  control over the validation process.
end note

App -> Domain: Build candidate
Domain --> App: Candidate
App -> Validator: Validate(candidate, selections, catalogue, requirements)
Validator -> Validator: Validate names/arguments and bind candidate
Validator -> Validator: Resolve prerequisites and execution order

alt Plan invalid or required coverage unsupported
    Validator --> App: Rejected or incomplete report with reason
else Plan executable
    loop Each resolved check, until blocking failure/incompletion
        Validator -> Client: Execute check against candidate
        Client -> MCP: tools/call(name, bound arguments)
        MCP --> Client: Structured result + checked values
        Client --> Validator: Validated tool result or execution error
        Validator -> Validator: Record evidence, scope, duration and candidate identity
    end
    Validator -> Validator: Assess evidence against acceptance requirements
    Validator --> App: Report + checked values
end

alt Rejected or incomplete
    App --> User: Failure or missing coverage + available evidence
    note right of User
      User may revise the prompt and start a new attempt.
      No automatic model repair loop in this workflow.
    end note
else Accepted within declared validation scope
    App -> Domain: Finalize(candidate, checked values, report)
    Domain --> App: Technically validated template
    App -> App: Attach prompt, model, catalogue, plan and evidence provenance
    App -> Domain: Generate representative questions using fixed seeds
    Domain --> App: Deterministic preview questions
    App --> User: Template + evidence + limitations + previews
    User -> App: Approve or reject
    alt User approves
        App -> App: Record approval for this exact artifact version
        User -> App: Generate question(template, seed)
        App -> Domain: Generate question(approved template, seed)
        Domain --> App: Deterministic question
        App --> User: Question
    else User rejects
        App -> App: Record decision; keep artifact unavailable to learners
    end
end

@enduml
